Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model made by Anthropic, prompted by Colin
Zwanziger, 10 November 2026. See the AI disclosure in
gist.RealCohesion.index.

The quotient of levels by finite chains.

Two levels are related, x ≈ y, if they are merely joined by a finite
chain of adjacent levels (gist.RealCohesion.FiniteChainLevels). As in
gist.RealCohesion.RealPathQuotient, we take ≈ to be the
proposition-valued symmetric, reflexive and transitive closure of
Relations.SRTclosure, so that no propositional resizing is involved.
Let Q be the quotient of the levels by ≈, with class map [_].

We use the large quotients of Quotient.Large, which TypeTopology
constructs from propositional truncations, function extensionality and
propositional extensionality. So Q needs no assumption beyond these.
It lives in 𝓤₁, the universe of the Dedekind reals, which is where we
need it.

Large quotients are effective. So if the class of a level x is the
class of the zero level, then x is merely joined to the zero level by
a chain of some length n, and x n ＝ ₀ by
gist.RealCohesion.FiniteChainLevels. This is how the finite-chain
lemma (gist.RealCohesion.FiniteChainLemma) obtains a natural number
from an equality in Q.

\begin{code}

{-# OPTIONS --safe --without-K #-}

open import MLTT.Spartan
open import UF.FunExt
open import UF.PropTrunc
open import UF.Subsingletons

module gist.RealCohesion.FiniteChainQuotient
        (fe : Fun-Ext)
        (pe : Prop-Ext)
        (pt : propositional-truncations-exist)
       where

open import UF.Sets
open import Quotient.Type using (EqRel)
open import Quotient.Large pt fe pe using (module large-quotient)
open import Relations.SRTclosure
open import gist.RealCohesion.FiniteChainLevels

open PropositionalTruncation pt

\end{code}

The equivalence relation generated by adjacency, and the quotient.

\begin{code}

_≈_ : Level → Level → 𝓤₀ ̇
_≈_ = psrt.psrt-closure pt Adj

chain-equivalence : EqRel {𝓤₀} {𝓤₀} Level
chain-equivalence = _≈_ , psrt.psrt-is-equiv-rel pt Adj

private
 module LQ = large-quotient Level chain-equivalence

Q : 𝓤₁ ̇
Q = LQ.X/≈

[_] : Level → Q
[_] = LQ.η

Q-is-set : is-set Q
Q-is-set = LQ.X/≈-is-set

Q-induction : {𝓦 : Universe} (P : Q → 𝓦 ̇ )
            → ((q : Q) → is-prop (P q))
            → ((x : Level) → P [ x ])
            → (q : Q) → P q
Q-induction = LQ.quotient-induction

adjacent-levels-have-the-same-class : (x y : Level) → Adj x y → [ x ] ＝ [ y ]
adjacent-levels-have-the-same-class x y a =
 LQ.η-identifies-related-points (psrt.psrt-extension pt Adj x y a)

\end{code}

Effectivity, and the zero bit. Because adjacency is symmetric, its
symmetric closure contains nothing new, and a chain in the symmetric
closure is a chain of adjacent levels.

\begin{code}

private
 s-closure-of-Adj-gives-Adj : (x y : Level) → s-closure Adj x y → Adj x y
 s-closure-of-Adj-gives-Adj x y (inl a) = a
 s-closure-of-Adj-gives-Adj x y (inr a) = Adj-is-symmetric y x a

 chains-of-s-closure : (n : ℕ) (x y : Level)
                     → iteration (s-closure Adj) n x y
                     → iteration Adj n x y
 chains-of-s-closure 0        x x refl        = refl
 chains-of-s-closure (succ n) x y (z , a , c) =
  z , s-closure-of-Adj-gives-Adj x z a , chains-of-s-closure n z y c

class-of-zero-gives-zero-bit : (x : Level)
                             → [ x ] ＝ [ zero-level ]
                             → ∃ n ꞉ ℕ , x n ＝ ₀
class-of-zero-gives-zero-bit x e =
 ∥∥-functor γ (LQ.η-relates-identified-points e)
 where
  γ : srt-closure Adj x zero-level → Σ n ꞉ ℕ , x n ＝ ₀
  γ (n , c) = n , chains-from-the-zero-level-end-with-a-zero n x
                   (iteration-symmetric Adj Adj-is-symmetric n x zero-level
                     (chains-of-s-closure n x zero-level c))

\end{code}
